  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "Paper Under Glass",
    "overview": "Two layers, never mixed. Content is calm, opaque, hairline-bordered paper: cards, tables, fields and empty states sit flat on a near-white cool ground. Everything that navigates or acts floats above that paper as Apple Liquid Glass: capsules and rounded slabs that blur, saturate and brighten what is behind them, with a specular rim that catches light from the top-left. The visual reference is binding (iOS 26 / macOS 26), and the kit refuses the category default of glass smeared on every card.\n\nDensity is dense-but-calm: a 4px grid, 36px default controls, 13-15px working text, and type that has to carry Thai tone marks and lower vowels without clipping. Soft colour fields sit behind the chrome so the glass has something to bend. Action is system blue; state is iOS-style green, amber and red, always tinted rather than filled.\n\nGlass is CSS only (blur + saturate + brightness + tint + sheen gradient + inset rim). Every material falls back to an opaque solid under `prefers-reduced-transparency: reduce` or `prefers-contrast: more`.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Opaque content layer, glass control layer; the boundary is the system.",
      "Three glass thicknesses: clear (controls over media), regular (sidebar, toolbar, tab bar), thick (menus, dialogs, tooltips, popovers).",
      "Capsule controls; concentric radii stepping down from 28px panels.",
      "Liquid press: glass and primary controls swell and brighten on a spring.",
      "Light and dark are both first-class; every material has a dark counterpart."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Tint, Not Fill, Rule",
        "body": "Status colour reaches the screen as a 12-20% tint with its darker `-text` partner. The only solid status fills are the switch \"on\" track and a highlighted destructive menu row.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Blue Rule",
        "body": "System blue is the only action colour. A second accent is not part of this system.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Tight Heading Rule",
        "body": "Headings track negative in steps (-0.01em, -0.015em, -0.03em) as size grows; body text keeps normal tracking.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Sixteen On Touch Rule",
        "body": "Text inputs are 16px below 768px and 14px above, so iOS Safari does not zoom on focus.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Two Layers Rule",
        "body": "Glass only on the control layer: nav, toolbars, tab bars, menus, selects, popovers, dialogs, tooltips, toasts. Cards, tables and fields stay opaque.",
        "section": "elevation"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Material Is Whole Rule",
        "body": "A glass surface carries no extra `bg-*`, `ring-1` or `shadow-*`; change a material through its `--glass-*` variables, not by stacking classes.",
        "section": "elevation"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Solid Fallback Rule",
        "body": "Every glass material drops blur and sheen and becomes `glass-solid` under reduced transparency or increased contrast.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do put glass only on what floats and acts: nav, toolbars, tab bars, menus, selects, popovers, dialogs, tooltips, toasts.",
      "Do pick the material by job: `glass-clear` over photos and media, `glass` for sidebars, toolbars and tab bars, `glass-thick` for anything with text to read.",
      "Do keep content opaque and flat: Card White, 1px hairline, no shadow.",
      "Do step radii down concentrically (28px, 21.6px, 16.8px, 12px) and make standalone controls capsules.",
      "Do give glass something to refract: place chrome over the `glass-backdrop` fields or real media.",
      "Do write status as a tint plus its darker `-text` partner.",
      "Do recompute WCAG ratios in both themes for any colour change; AA on every glass material is a product requirement.",
      "Do respect `prefers-reduced-motion` (press and spring transitions drop to 0ms) and keep the solid glass fallback."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't use glass on cards, tables, fields or other content-layer surfaces.",
      "Don't add `bg-*`, `ring-1` or `shadow-*` to a glass surface, or stack two glass classes; tune the `--glass-*` variables instead.",
      "Don't add a second accent colour or fill status colours solid on large areas.",
      "Don't use SVG displacement or `backdrop-filter: url()` refraction; it is Chromium-only and costly.",
      "Don't use type styles that clip Thai tone marks or lower vowels: no line-height below 1.25 on text that can be Thai."
    ]
  }
}
